# Product Details Page Implementation Plan

This plan outlines the architecture and tasks required to build a premium, responsive Product Details page for the AgriChain marketplace, including backend API extensions and comprehensive React components.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Cart & Wishlist Mocking:** The endpoints `POST /api/cart`, `POST /api/wishlist`, and `POST /api/contact-farmer` will be implemented as mocked endpoints (returning success responses without deep state management) since full cart and messaging systems are usually standalone modules.
> **Blockchain Verification:** The `GET /api/blockchain/verify/:id` endpoint will simulate Arbitrum smart contract verification by returning formatted mock verification data (hash, block number, timestamp) based on the product's `blockchain_hash`.
> **Reviews:** We will create a new MongoDB collection and model for `reviews` to demonstrate the rating distributions and review cards correctly.

## Open Questions
- Do you have a specific Arbitrum testnet explorer URL format you want to use for the "View on Arbiscan" button (e.g., `https://sepolia.arbiscan.io/tx/...`), or should I use a generic placeholder?
- For the QR Code generation, should the backend generate an actual image (Base64), or should it just return the data payload and let the React frontend generate the QR visual using `qrcode.react` (which is already in package.json)? I strongly recommend the latter for performance and crispness.

